          "date": "2026-10-22 03:46:22.000000000",
          "tz": 600
        },
        "subject": "LU-21014 lod: keep EC raid sets on distinct OSTs in RR",
        "message": "LU-21014 lod: keep EC raid sets on distinct OSTs in RR\n\nWith overstriping, lod_check_and_reserve_ost() lets the RR loop reuse\nan OST while lag_ost_avail says unique OSTs remain. That count includes\nOSTs RR skips, such as inactive or degraded ones, so an EC data\ncomponent can reuse an OST before lod_ec_add_data() takes over, which\nrepeats the placed stripes assuming they are unique and so puts two\nstripes of a raid set on one OST, e.g. -C 13 --ec 5+2 on 8 OSTs with\none down.\n\nLeave all OST reuse for EC components to lod_ec_add_data() and\nlod_ec_add_parities(), which keep each raid set on distinct OSTs.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5\nChange-Id: I8fe6431de113351e92653780fe17db2e8a180697\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
